              "text": "संभलकर (sambhalkar) — \"carefully\", \"steadily\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "संभलकर (sambhalkar) जाना — \"go carefully\", said to someone setting out after dark or in the rain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "संभलकर (sambhalkar) is sambhalnā, \"to steady oneself\", with -kar, \"having\". CDIAL lists the verb under Sanskrit saṁbharati, \"brings together\", and its causing form \"maintains\" (CDIAL 12961)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A second way to wish someone safe."
